BT /F2 15 Tf 48 795 Td (FORMULA AND EQUATION REFERENCE) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 48 771.7 Td (Chapter-specific equations worth knowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 758.9000000000001 Td (- Vector components: A_x=A cos\(theta\); A_y=A sin\(theta\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 747.0000000000001 Td (- Perpendicular resultant magnitude: R = sqrt\(A_x^2 + A_y^2\); direction theta = tan^-1\(A_y/A_x\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 735.1000000000001 Td (- Angular speed: omega = v/r; centripetal acceleration a_c = v^2/r = r omega^2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 723.2000000000002 Td (- Projectile components: u_x=u cos\(theta\); u_y=u sin\(theta\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 711.3000000000002 Td (- For launch and landing at the same height: T=2u sin\(theta\)/g; H=u^2 sin^2\(theta\)/\(2g\); R=u^2 sin\(2theta\)/g.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 699.4000000000002 Td (- Vertical drop from rest: h=\(1/2\)gt^2; horizontal launch flight time t=sqrt\(2h/g\); horizontal range = u_x t.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 687.5000000000002 Td (- Angular conversion: 1 revolution = 2pi radians; omega=2pi f.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 48 675.6000000000003 Td (Use each equation only when its assumptions apply; keep units consistent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 430 24 Td (StudyNest | Page 2 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
